WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.953
FFmpeg's new release

00:00:01.765 --> 00:00:03.227
signs with post-quantum

00:00:03.039 --> 00:00:03.663
keys

00:00:04.182 --> 00:00:06.682
FFmpeg 9.1 codenamed

00:00:06.493 --> 00:00:07.071
Gauss

00:00:07.248 --> 00:00:08.097
is the latest

00:00:07.908 --> 00:00:08.733
release of the

00:00:08.604 --> 00:00:10.207
open-source multimedia

00:00:10.019 --> 00:00:10.762
framework

00:00:10.927 --> 00:00:11.717
which ships a

00:00:11.529 --> 00:00:12.755
new major version

00:00:12.566 --> 00:00:13.073
about

00:00:13.097 --> 00:00:14.347
every six months

00:00:14.878 --> 00:00:16.694
FFmpeg only provides

00:00:16.505 --> 00:00:17.295
source code

00:00:17.413 --> 00:00:18.734
so ready-to-run builds

00:00:18.545 --> 00:00:19.382
come from other

00:00:19.194 --> 00:00:20.420
providers linked on

00:00:20.232 --> 00:00:21.304
the download page

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:23.575
Releases are cryptographically

00:00:23.387 --> 00:00:24.070
signed

00:00:24.141 --> 00:00:25.061
and the newest

00:00:24.896 --> 00:00:26.405
also carry post-quantum

00:00:26.217 --> 00:00:27.808
signatures that GnuPG

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:28.846
cannot verify yet

00:00:28.658 --> 00:00:29.672
you need sq

00:00:29.483 --> 00:00:31.075
1.4 or later

00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:32.628
Full story on

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:33.335
the dashboard
